<resources>
    <!--
        The logo's ink, for the one place the app draws the logo itself.

        The only fixed colour in a UI that is otherwise Material's, and from
        Android 12 the wallpaper's. That is deliberate and is the usual exception:
        a logo is the thing on a screen that does not follow the user's accent
        colour, because a mark that arrives in a different colour on each phone is
        not a mark. Everything around it still themes normally.

        It is a shade deeper than the taupe on the printed logo, which is
        letterpressed into cream and can afford to be faint. This one has to hold
        its own on a white surface and on a dark one — it clears 4:1 against both
        of Material's defaults — and at 40dp, which is smaller than a logo is ever
        printed.
    -->
    <color name="brand_ink">#96795E</color>
</resources>
